# Brand colors (do not revert)

This app uses a **blue primary** on a **white / neutral gray** surface. Do **not** restore the old teal/green palette.

## Canonical tokens (`resources/css/app.css` `:root`)

| Token | Required value | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `--primary` | `hsl(221 83% 53%)` | Brand blue (Tailwind blue-600 family) |
| `--ring` / `--sidebar-primary` / `--chart-1` | same as `--primary` | Keep in sync |
| `--background` | `hsl(0 0% 100%)` | Pure white |
| `--sidebar-background` / `--sidebar` | `hsl(0 0% 100%)` | Pure white |
| Neutrals (`--secondary`, `--muted`, `--border`, `--input`) | `hsl(0 0% …)` | No green or blue tint |

## Forbidden

- Teal/green brand hues (~150–175), e.g. `hsl(175 72% 28%)`, `hsl(160 18% 97%)`
- Tinted page backgrounds (mint, sage, pale teal, pale blue wash)
- Hardcoded `via-[hsl(175_…)]` / `to-[hsl(152_…)]` / `bg-teal-*` brand accents

## Allowed green

Semantic success only (`text-green-600`, emerald status badges, sonner success). Not for primary buttons, links, sidebar active, or brand chrome.

## Related files

- `resources/views/app.blade.php` html bootstrap: `background-color: hsl(0 0% 100%);`
- Auth split panel gradient must stay blue (`hsl(221…)` / `hsl(224…)`)
- Guarded by `tests/Feature/ThemeColorsTest.php` — do not weaken or delete that test
- `resources/views/app.blade.php` also re-declares brand tokens **after** `@vite` so Cloudflare/browser CSS cache cannot keep an old teal `--primary`
